  "algorithms": [
    {
      "name": "Interleaving Distance via the Supremum-of-Gaps Isometry",
      "description": "Computes the interleaving distance between two filtrations by exploiting the Bridge VIII isometry, which collapses the defining infimum over scale-shifts into a single supremum over simplices: d(F, G) = max over all simplices sigma of |F.weight(sigma) - G.weight(sigma)|. For finitely supported weights (the simplices of a finite complex) this is a single linear sweep, with arithmetic complexity O(|S|) where |S| is the number of simplices. It is the computational backbone for every metric corollary of Bridge X, since each law is, after the isometry, a statement about scaled and summed copies of this single number.",
      "pseudocode": "function interleaving_distance(F, G):\n    best <- 0\n    S <- support(F) union support(G)\n    for sigma in S:\n        gap <- | F.weight(sigma) - G.weight(sigma) |\n        best <- max(best, gap)\n    return best",
      "code": "from typing import Dict, FrozenSet\n\nWeight = Dict[FrozenSet[int], float]\n\n\ndef interleaving_distance(F: Weight, G: Weight) -> float:\n    \"\"\"d(F, G) = sup over simplices of |F.weight(s) - G.weight(s)|.\"\"\"\n    keys = set(F) | set(G)\n    return max((abs(F.get(s, 0.0) - G.get(s, 0.0)) for s in keys), default=0.0)\n"
    },
    {
      "name": "Convex-Interpolation Geodesic with O(1) Affine Reparametrization",
      "description": "Builds the constant-speed geodesic lerp(F, G, t) by pointwise convex combination (1 - t)*F + t*G of the weight functions, valid for t in [0, 1] because a convex combination of grounded, monotone weights is grounded and monotone. The affine gluing law (lerp_lerp) gives an O(1) reparametrization rule: the geodesic nested between two interior points lerp(F,G,s) and lerp(F,G,t), evaluated at rate r, equals lerp(F, G, (1-r)*s + r*t) directly, so nested interpolations never require materializing intermediate filtrations. This is the computational shadow of local-to-global coherence.",
      "pseudocode": "function lerp(F, G, t):           # t in [0, 1]\n    for sigma in support(F) union support(G):\n        P.weight(sigma) <- (1 - t) * F.weight(sigma) + t * G.weight(sigma)\n    return P\n\nfunction nested_param(r, s, t):   # gluing law reparametrization\n    return (1 - r) * s + r * t     # lerp(lerp s, lerp t, r) = lerp((1-r)s+rt)",
      "code": "from typing import Dict, FrozenSet\n\nWeight = Dict[FrozenSet[int], float]\n\n\ndef lerp(F: Weight, G: Weight, t: float) -> Weight:\n    \"\"\"Constant-speed geodesic (1 - t) * F + t * G, valid for t in [0, 1].\"\"\"\n    assert -1e-9 <= t <= 1.0 + 1e-9\n    keys = set(F) | set(G)\n    return {s: (1.0 - t) * F.get(s, 0.0) + t * G.get(s, 0.0) for s in keys}\n\n\ndef nested_param(r: float, s: float, t: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Gluing law: lerp(lerp s, lerp t, r) = lerp(F, G, (1-r)*s + r*t).\"\"\"\n    return (1.0 - r) * s + r * t\n"
    }
